      "message": "It seems to me gemini uses socket.inet_aton, apply only if it is feasible.\n```\n\ndef construct_arp_packet(src_mac, dst_mac, src_ip, dst_ip, op) -\u003e str:\n  \"\"\"\n  Constructs an ARP packet as a hex string.\n\n  Args:\n    src_mac: Source MAC address (e.g., \"11:22:33:44:55:66\")\n    dst_mac: Destination MAC address (e.g., \"aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff\")\n    src_ip: Source IP address (e.g., \"192.168.1.100\")\n    dst_ip: Destination IP address (e.g., \"192.168.1.1\")\n    op: ARP operation code (1 for request, 2 for reply)\n\n  Returns:\n    A hex string representing the ARP packet.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  import struct\n  import socket\n\n  # Ethernet header\n  eth_header \u003d struct.pack(\n      \"!6s6sH\",\n      bytes.fromhex(dst_mac.replace(\":\", \"\")),\n      bytes.fromhex(src_mac.replace(\":\", \"\")),\n      0x0806,  # EtherType for ARP\n  )\n\n  # ARP header\n  arp_header \u003d struct.pack(\n      \"!HHBBH6s4s6s4s\",\n      1,  # Hardware type (Ethernet \u003d 1)\n      0x0800,  # Protocol type (IPv4 \u003d 0x0800)\n      6,  # Hardware address length (6 bytes for MAC)\n      4,  # Protocol address length (4 bytes for IPv4)\n      op,  # Operation code (1 for request, 2 for reply)\n      bytes.fromhex(src_mac.replace(\":\", \"\")),\n      socket.inet_aton(src_ip),\n      bytes.fromhex(dst_mac.replace(\":\", \"\")),\n      socket.inet_aton(dst_ip),\n  )\n\n  # Combine headers\n  arp_packet \u003d eth_header + arp_header\n\n  # Convert to hex string\n  hex_packet \u003d arp_packet.hex()\n\n  return hex_packet\n```",
